I also need a new winter coat.
I look at the coats in the shop.
I find a beautiful, green coat.
It is very thick.
I put the coat on.
Now I have the green coat on.
I look in a large mirror.
The coat is unfortunately too small.
It is very tight across the shoulders.
I take it off again.
The shop assistant comes over to me.
"Is the coat too tight?" she asks.
"Yes, it is too small," I answer.
"Do you have a large size?" I ask.
The shop assistant checks on the computer.
"No, unfortunately we do not have a large size," she says.
"We only have small sizes left."
"That is fine," I say.
I hang the green coat back in place.
I do not buy it.
